# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
EN = {
    "tech2_pneumatic": {
        "title": "PneumaticCraft", "subtitle": "Pressure, plastic and drones you program yourself",
        "intro": [
            "PneumaticCraft is the only mod in the pack where a machine can explode simply because you pumped too much air into it. Pressure is a real resource here: scarce, slow to build and instant to lose.",
            "At the end of the road stand drones — small robots you draw a program for out of instruction blocks and send off to dig, build, harvest or fight.",
            "It all starts with compressed iron: you put iron ingots in a fire and blow them up.",
        ],
        "quests": {
            "compressed": {"title": "Compressed Iron", "text": [
                "Drop iron ingots on the ground and set off TNT. About a fifth burns away entirely; the rest survives as compressed iron, the mod's base material.",
                "The method is crude but works from day one and needs nothing but explosives. Later the pressure chamber does the same thing with no losses at all, and blowing up ingots stops being worth it.",
                "One trick for later: compress blocks of iron, not ingots. Moving an item through the chamber interface costs the same either way, and a block holds nine times as much."]},
            "compressor": {"title": "Air Compressor", "text": [
                "Burns fuel and drives air into tubes. The manometer shows pressure, and it's worth watching: an ordinary tube lives to five bar and bursts for certain past seven.",
                "An open tube end hisses and bleeds air the faster the higher the pressure. The pneumatic wrench closes off the sides you don't want, the safety module vents the excess on its own, and the regulator module bridges networks of different tiers.",
                "The blast is weak but the block vanishes without a drop. The check happens only while air is flowing in: a machine left over-pressured with the supply cut will not go off."]},
            "chamber": {"title": "Pressure Chamber", "text": [
                "A hollow cube of glass walls with a valve and an interface. Three, four or five blocks to a side, nothing but air inside. Under pressure it runs recipes found nowhere else: empty circuit boards, transistors, acid, diamonds out of coal blocks.",
                "The chamber is also a battery: a five-by-five cube holds four hundred and thirty-two thousand millibuckets of air, enough to ride out any spike in demand.",
                "Negative pressure inside pulls enchantments off an item and into a book. That is how you get the books for the jackhammer, which no enchanting table will touch.",
                "It's the mod's first multiblock and its most necessary."]},
            "plastic": {"title": "Plastic", "text": [
                "The refinery breaks crude oil into diesel, kerosene, gasoline and LPG, and the taller the stack, the more fractions come out of a single pass. The oil comes from Immersive Petroleum wells or your own drilling.",
                "LPG and a lump of coal in the thermopneumatic processing plant give liquid plastic; freeze it down to zero in a heat frame and you have a sheet.",
                "Plastic goes into everything: boards, drones, armor."]},
            "pcb": {"title": "Printed Circuit Boards", "text": [
                "An empty board, UV exposure, an acid etch — and you have a finished board. A full exposure takes up to ten minutes and yields every board; pull them early and some come out as rejects.",
                "Rejects aren't wasted: a blast furnace melts them back into empty boards.",
                "One detail can stall the whole branch: the blueprint for the UV light box cannot be crafted. You order it on an Amadron tablet for eight emeralds, or buy it from a mechanic villager.",
                "Boards are the heart of all the mod's electronics."]},
            "assembly": {"title": "Assembly Line", "text": [
                "A controller, a platform, a drill and a laser — a conveyor that manufactures parts to a program. Only the controller takes air; the rest feed off it.",
                "The programs, like the board blueprint, are not craftable: drill and laser cost eight emeralds each on the Amadron tablet, the combined one fourteen.",
                "The line is what all of this was for: a block of compressed iron under the drill gives twenty valves, and those valves under the laser give eight advanced tubes. There is no other road to tier two tubing."]},
            "drone": {"title": "Drone", "text": [
                "The programmer draws the drone a task out of instruction blocks: go here, dig this, put it there, repeat.",
                "The GPS tool sets coordinates. Logistics drones move items around your base without a single pipe."]},
            "armor": {"title": "Pneumatic Armor", "text": [
                "The helmet shows mobs and chests through walls, the chestplate pulls items in with a magnet and soaks up lava damage, the leggings lengthen your stride and your jump, the boots hold jet thrust.",
                "Upgrades are installed at the charging station and run on the same compressed air, and each one binds its own key. Sort that layout out on the ground before your first flight.",
                "Jet boots come in five tiers. Tier three adds builder mode, a strictly vertical climb; tier four adds stabilizers that kill your speed the moment you let go of the thrust. A separate upgrade puts an elytra in the chestplate that never spends durability."]},
            "elevator": {"title": "Elevator", "text": ["A pneumatic elevator rises to any height and is called by a button on each floor. Quiet, fast and without a single piston."]},
        },
    },
    "tech2_foregoing": {
        "title": "Industrial Foregoing", "subtitle": "Latex, lasers and farms that run themselves",
        "intro": [
            "Industrial Foregoing is a set of machines with no single chain: each does one job and does it well. Plants, harvests, milks, shears, kills, smelts, stores.",
            "It starts with latex tapped out of logs and ends with a laser that fires into bedrock and pulls ore back out without a single pickaxe.",
        ],
        "quests": {
            "latex": {"title": "Latex", "text": [
                "The tree fluid extractor taps latex from logs, the processing unit boils it into dry rubber, and rubber becomes plastic.",
                "Plastic is the material of every frame and half the mod's machines."]},
            "frames": {"title": "Machine Frames", "text": [
                "Four tiers: pity, simple, advanced, supreme. Each machine wants a frame of its tier, and that's the mod's only progression."]},
            "farm": {"title": "Auto Farm", "text": [
                "The sower plants across an area, the gatherer harvests everything it can reach, whole trees included.",
                "The mod's fertilizer speeds growth. The farm ends up compact and fully autonomous."]},
            "animals": {"title": "Ranching", "text": [
                "The rancher milks cows and shears sheep without touching the animals. The feeder breeds them automatically.",
                "The slaughter factory and mob crusher turn a farm into a source of meat, experience and pink slime."]},
            "ore_meat": {"title": "Meat Metallurgy", "text": [
                "The strangest ore processing in the pack: ore is washed in meat, aged in a fermenter and sieved into dust.",
                "The yield is three to five ingots per ore, depending on how long it aged. The fermentation station wants a hot block below it and a cold one beside it."]},
            "laser": {"title": "Laser Drilling", "text": [
                "The laser base fires into bedrock and pulls ore back out. Lenses decide which ore: the rarer it is, the more lenses of the right colour you need.",
                "It's an endless source of any resource and the main reason to install the mod."]},
            "stonework": {"title": "Stonework Factory", "text": ["One machine that turns water and lava into cobble, stone, brick, glass and everything cut from them. Placed once, it feeds construction for the rest of the game."]},
        },
    },
    "tech2_powah": {
        "title": "Powah", "subtitle": "Energy without complications: generators, cells, reactor",
        "intro": [
            "Powah invents no mechanics — it delivers energy simply and reliably. Five kinds of generator, cells of any size, cables and wireless transfer.",
            "Everything comes in five tiers: starter, basic, hardened, blazing, niotic, spirited and nitro. Only the numbers change, but they change fast.",
        ],
        "quests": {
            "dielectric": {"title": "Dielectric", "text": ["Paste, rods and casing — everything in this mod is built from them. Plus energized steel, made in the energizing orb."]},
            "generators": {"title": "Generators", "text": [
                "The thermo generator on temperature difference, the furnator on coal, the magmator on lava, the solar panel on sunlight.",
                "Every starter version is cheap and goes up the first evening."]},
            "cells": {"title": "Cells and Cables", "text": [
                "The cell stores, the cable carries. The ender cell links two points without wire, the player transmitter charges everything in your pockets at range."]},
            "energizing": {"title": "Energizing Orb", "text": [
                "The orb and the rods around it turn energy into materials: energized steel, crystals, higher-tier components.",
                "More rods, faster work. It's the mod's hub machine."]},
            "crystals": {"title": "Crystals", "text": [
                "Blazing, niotic, spirited, nitro — four crystals that set the tier of all the tech.",
                "Made in the orb from matching materials, and they aren't cheap."]},
            "reactor": {"title": "Reactor", "text": [
                "Uraninite is mined underground and feeds the reactor. Multiblock, quiet and very strong — but it needs cooling.",
                "Fuel burns slowly and the output depends on neither sun nor coal."]},
        },
    },
    "tech2_petroleum": {
        "title": "Immersive Petroleum", "subtitle": "Oil, wells and what's distilled from them",
        "intro": [
            "An Immersive Engineering addon that gives it an oil industry: survey, drilling, extraction and refining.",
            "Oil sits in reservoirs under whole regions. Finding one is half the job; the other half is building a pumpjack over it.",
        ],
        "quests": {
            "survey": {"title": "Survey", "text": [
                "The seismic survey tool tells you whether a reservoir lies under this area and what kind. The Immersive Engineering core sample does the same for ore.",
                "A reservoir is not tied to a chunk, it stretches across a whole region, and drilling blind is still pointless: over empty ground a derrick stands without a single drop.",
                "Every survey shot eats a buckshot cartridge and reads a square sixty-five blocks on a side."]},
            "derrick": {"title": "Derrick", "text": [
                "The derrick opens the reservoir, and the first thing it does is gush: up to two and a half buckets a tick until the upper half of the deposit is gone. That pressure never comes back, so put the tanks up before you drill.",
                "The derrick is placed once per field and works until the field runs dry."]},
            "pumpjack": {"title": "Pumpjack", "text": [
                "The famous nodding donkey. Once the gusher dies down, the pumpjack lifts the second half of the deposit, with no pressure behind it at all, fifteen millibuckets a tick.",
                "Reservoirs aren't infinite, but they never quite die either: a spent oil well stays a source of six millibuckets a tick forever. Too little for a plant, enough to keep the spot on the map from becoming junk."]},
            "tower": {"title": "Distillation Tower", "text": [
                "Oil splits into fractions: gasoline, diesel, lubricant, bitumen. Each goes its own way.",
                "The flarestack burns off surplus gas so the tower doesn't stall."]},
            "products": {"title": "Products", "text": [
                "Asphalt makes roads you run faster on. Lubricant speeds up Immersive Engineering machines through the auto lubricator.",
                "Napalm is for when diplomacy didn't work."]},
        },
    },
}
